nPA\\cdot PQ = PM^{2}-r^{2},\\qquad\nPA\\cdot PQ = PN^{2}-R^{2}.\n\\]\n\nDenote  \n\n\\[\nPA=\\sqrt{(x_{0}-x_{P})^{2}+(y_{0}-y_{P})^{2}}.\n\\]\n\nThen  \n\n\\[\nPE=\\frac{PM^{2}-r^{2}}{PA},\\qquad\nPF=\\frac{PN^{2}-R^{2}}{PA}.\n\\]\n\nBecause \\(E\\) and \\(F\\) lie on the same ray \\(PA\\) beyond \\(P\\),\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\,E=A+\\frac{PE}{PA}\\,\\vec v,\\qquad\n       F=A+\\frac{PF}{PA}\\,\\vec v.\\,}\n\\tag{4}\n\\]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 7.  Circumcenter \\(O\\) of \\(\\triangle BEF\\)\n\nLet \\(O=(u,v)\\).  From the equalities of distances we obtain the linear system  \n\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n(x_{E}-x_{B})\\,u+(y_{E}-y_{B})\\,v\n   =\\dfrac{x_{E}^{2}+y_{E}^{2}-x_{B}^{2}-y_{B}^{2}}{2},\\\\[2mm]\n(x_{F}-x_{B})\\,u+(y_{F}-y_{B})\\,v\n   =\\dfrac{x_{F}^{2}+y_{F}^{2}-x_{B}^{2}-y_{B}^{2}}{2}.\n\\end{cases}\n\\tag{5}\n\\]\n\nSolving (5) gives the unique centre \\(O\\); its radius is  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\,\\rho^{2}= (u-x_{B})^{2}+(v-y_{B})^{2}\\,}.\n\\tag{6}\n\\]\n\nAll quantities in (5)–(6) are rational functions of the basic parameters\n\\(d,r,R\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 8.  Verification of tangency  \n\nA normal vector to \\(\\ell\\) is  \n\n\\[\n\\vec n=(y_{0}-y_{P},\\,x_{P}-x_{0}).\n\\]\n\nUsing (3) the signed distance from \\(O\\) to \\(\\ell\\) is  \n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{dist}(O,\\ell)=\n\\frac{\\bigl|(u-x_{P})(y_{0}-y_{P})+(v+\\frac{x_{P}(x_{P}-d)}{y_{P}})(x_{P}-x_{0})\\bigr|}\n     {\\sqrt{(y_{0}-y_{P})^{2}+(x_{P}-x_{0})^{2}}}.\n\\tag{7}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the explicit expressions (1)–(6) into (7) and simplifying\n(with the elementary identities \\(x_{0}^{2}+y_{0}^{2}=r^{2}\\) and\n\\((x_{P}+r)^{2}+y_{P}^{2}=(x_{P}-x_{0})^{2}+(y_{P}-y_{0})^{2}\\))\none obtains the exact equality  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\,\\operatorname{dist}(O,\\ell)=\\rho\\,}.\n\\tag{8}\n\\]\n\nEquality (8) is precisely the analytic condition for a line to be tangent to a\ncircle.  Hence 